  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 144 PM EDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nThe main story for the extended period will be rising temperatures \nand the potential for impactful heat late this week into the \nupcoming weekend. The set up responsible for these trends will be an \neastward migrating mid-level ridge, currently over the Desert \nSouthwest and high pressure at the surface. Temperatures are \nforecast to rise to the upper 80s to low 90s (outside of the higher \nelevations) by Wednesday, with temperatures trending upward a degree \nor two each day going forward. Increasing moisture will support the \nreturn of dewpoints in the mid-to-upper 70s and PWs in excess of \n1.5\". Thus, heat index values ('feels like' temperatures) return to \ntriple digit values for most places heading into the next weekend. \nHeat headlines may be necessary in future forecasts. In the \nmeantime, be mindful of the heat as you plan for any outdoor work or \nactivities over the next 7 days.\n\nAny disturbances that translate through the the mid/upper level flow \nmay act to locally enhance thunderstorm activity on any given day. A \nfew MCSs (thunderstorm complexes) look to pass just to our north and \neast over the next few days but could clip parts of Northeast \nGA...something to watch as models generally struggle with the \nevolution of these features. Otherwise, expect at least low chances \n(20-30%) for afternoon and evening thunderstorms over the next 5-7 \ndays.",
